{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And on the day when raw flesh is seen.</b> Rashi explained: even though it is spelled out in Kiddushin that a nega and michiah do not impart impurity in the twenty-four extremities of limbs — because it requires 'according to all the appearance of the eyes of the priest' — the verse comes to say that if a nega spreads in them to the point that it is exposed and plainly visible, such as when it healed in fat and the head of the limb became broad, it is impure. But he was not precise, for superficially it does not deal with what is exposed; rather, michiah or a nega imparts impurity in the extremities of limbs alone — this is a decree of the King, that it is a sign of impurity, just as with other flesh that is susceptible to impurity through negaim, that if it is exposed in it, it returns to impurity. And so it implies in Torat Kohanim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:06.604478125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}